{{Italic title|string=Hercules: The Legendary Journeys}}
''[[Hercules: The Legendary Journeys]]'' is a television series that was filmed in New Zealand<ref>{{cite book |last1=Elmer |first1=Greg |last2=Davis |first2=Charles H. |last3=Marchessault |first3=Janine |last4=McCullough |first4=John |title=Locating Migrating Media |date=10 July 2012 |publisher=Lexington Books |isbn=978-0-7391-4243-1 |page=120 |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=Pr7RR-MIfBsC&pg=PA120 |language=en}}</ref> and the United States, starring [[Kevin Sorbo]] as [[Heracles|Hercules]]. It is very loosely based on the tales of the classical [[Greek mythology|Greek]] [[culture hero]] [[Heracles]]. It ran for 111 episodes over six seasons.

It was preceded by several TV movies with the same major characters in 1994 as part of [[Universal Television|Universal Media Studios]]'s [[Action Pack (TV programming block)|Action Pack]]: in order, ''[[Hercules and the Amazon Women]]'', ''[[Hercules and the Lost Kingdom]]'', ''[[Hercules and the Circle of Fire]]'', ''[[Hercules in the Underworld]]'', and ''[[Hercules in the Maze of the Minotaur]]'', the last of which served mostly as a "[[clip show]]" of the previous movies as a lead up to the series.
{{TOC right}}

